Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the comparison `b.url === inc.url` treated URLs as raw strings, so case differences in the hostname (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com`) weren't recognized as the same URL.

**Fix:** added a `normalizeUrl` helper that lowercases the hostname via `new URL(url).href` (falling back to the raw string for unparseable input), and now compares `normalizeUrl(b.url) === normalizeUrl(inc.url)`.

Verified with a temporary test (now removed): case-differing URLs merge into the existing entry with unioned tags, and unrelated URLs still append. Only `src/import_merge.ts` changed.


